      Each metric ranked by how much it shifted from initial → recovery at matched watts. Direction-aware: a metric where lower-is-better (HR, RR, VE) gets ranked by how much it rose; higher-is-better metrics (TV, fat oxidation, watts/breath) by how much they fell. <strong>Top of the list = the system that limited recovery performance most.</strong> Use the ▲▼ arrows to override the data-driven ranking with your own clinical judgement; your order persists across sessions.
